      "end_timestamp": "02:02",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Codeine. It makes me throw up, terribly.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:03",
      "end_timestamp": "02:07",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Noted. And what's your health history, besides the cholesterol?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:10",
      "end_timestamp": "02:15",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.surgical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "High cholesterol, that's why I'm here. And I had my gallbladder out, years ago. About 2012.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:17",
      "end_timestamp": "02:25",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.surgical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Pulse 70, temperature 36.6.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:48",
      "end_timestamp": "02:51",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Good strength. Your thigh muscles aren't tender when I press them.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:24",
      "end_timestamp": "03:30",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Your strength is normal, and that's reassuring. The aches and tiredness could be a statin side effect, so I'd say statin-related muscle aches are likely.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:38",
      "end_timestamp": "03:53",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'd like to arrange a blood test for muscle enzymes, called CK, and check your thyroid, because an underactive thyroid can mimic this.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:00",
      "end_timestamp": "04:14",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Not yet, wait for the results, but if the aches become severe or your urine goes dark, stop and ring us at once.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:22",
      "end_timestamp": "04:34",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
